Cell["\<\
The arity is the number of cyclic words the obstruction takes before the \
pairing object, and it is what a sweep uses to build its tuples.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1ceb4d4c-e752-436d-8e66-caeec29f595e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["$DefiningIdentities"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/$DefiningIdentities", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b5e78cf8-951b-49a7-ac27-5255e7bbe5c2"],
 " is a plain value, not a held registry: adding an entry to a copy of it is \
enough to sweep an identity of one's own, provided the function follows the \
same calling convention of ",
 StyleBox["arity", "TI"],
 " words followed by the pairing object."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5f6ebf06-2ddf-4ab4-9d95-70c48b681aab"]
}, Open  ]],

